# Guard mode

Combine the practices in the installed `careful` and `freeze` skills. Read both, reuse the user's stated directory and authorization, then apply their destructive-operation review and resolved-path boundary to all mutations.

In Codex and DevSpace these are advisory instructions, not newly installed enforcement. Do not claim that hooks are running or that writes are mechanically blocked without verified host registration and coverage. Existing host protections remain independent. Report the selected directory and actual enforcement level accurately.

Use `/unfreeze` to clear the requested edit boundary; honor a request to end careful review separately. Do not assume a persistent freeze state file disappears when the conversation ends.
